    "statementMarkdown": "Let $P$ be a set of $n \\geqslant 3$ points in the plane, no three of which are on a line. How many possibilities are there to choose a set $T$ of $\\left(\\begin{array}{c}n-1 \\\\ 2\\end{array}\\right)$ triangles, whose vertices are all in $P$, such that each triangle in $T$ has a side that is not a side of any other triangle in $T$ ?\n",
